        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: قصه",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قصه (qesse) — \"a tale, a story\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مادربزرگم هر شب برای ما قصه میگفت. Mâdarbozorgam har shab barâ-ye mâ qesse migoft. Every night my grandmother used to tell us a story."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Close to dâstân, but often a folk tale told aloud. Qesse goftan \"to tell a tale\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "qesse is borrowed from Arabic qiṣṣa, \"story\" (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
