          "title": "You'll want to know: یکی بود یکی نبود",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "یکی بود یکی نبود (yeki bud yeki nabud) — \"there was one and there was none (the opening of a folk tale)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قصه (qesse) با یکی بود یکی نبود شروع شد. Qesse bâ yeki bud yeki nabud shoru' shod. The tale began with There was one, there was none."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The traditional opening of a Persian folk tale, often followed by gheyr az khodâ hich-kas nabud \"and apart from God there was nobody\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "yeki bud yeki nabud is built from native Persian words only: yeki \"one\", bud \"was\" and nabud \"was not\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
